Statements:
[
    "Faithfulness is a metric that uses an LLM as a judge to measure whether a generator’s output is aligned with the retrieved context.",
    "Faithfulness works by extracting factual claims from the model’s response and checking each claim against the retrieval context.",
    "All claims are extracted from the response, optionally with a truth-extraction limit.",
    "Each claim is compared to the retrieved context.",
    "Each claim is assigned one of three verdicts: "yes", "no", or "I don't know".",
    ""yes" means grounded and came from the context.",
    ""no" means hallucination and not from the context.",
    ""I don't know" means ambiguous or unverifiable.",
    "A claim is considered truthful if it does not contradict any facts in the retrieval context.",
    "Faithfulness score is calculated as the number of grounded (yes) claims divided by the total number of extracted claims.",
    "In the example, 10 claims total and 8 grounded produce a score of 0.8.",
    "A score of 0.8 corresponds to 20% hallucination.",
    "Including or excluding ambiguous "I don't know" claims in the denominator changes the score.",
    "The truth-extraction limit or whether to count ambiguous claims can be adjusted."
] 

